        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find the derivative of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x) = \\ln(x^2-4).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find the derivative of [MATH: f(x) = \\ln(x^2-4).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)]</span> as the composite function</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f = \\ln u, \\qquad u = x^2-4.]</span></p><p>Differentiating gives</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{u},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = 2x.]</span></p><p>We now apply the chain rule, and we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (1)/(u) \u22c5 2x; = (1)/(x^{2} \u2212 4) \u22c5 2x; = (2x)/(x^{2} \u2212 4).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we express [MATH: f(x)] as the composite function\n\n[MATH: f = \\ln u, \\qquad u = x^2-4.]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{u},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = 2x.]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (1)/(u) \u22c5 2x; = (1)/(x^{2} \u2212 4) \u22c5 2x; = (2x)/(x^{2} \u2212 4).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind the derivative of [MATH: f(x) = \\ln(x^2-4).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we express [MATH: f(x)] as the composite function\n\n[MATH: f = \\ln u, \\qquad u = x^2-4.]\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = \\dfrac{1}{u},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d x} = 2x.]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n[MATH: (df)/(dx)|= (df)/(du) \u22c5 (du)/(dx); = (1)/(u) \u22c5 2x; = (1)/(x^{2} \u2212 4) \u22c5 2x; = (2x)/(x^{2} \u2212 4).]"
      },
